Within the matching models, models I, P and Q match the inferred \\mathcal{R}_{\\rm BHNS} that is based on a broader BHNS mass distribution, whereas the matching model J variations overlap only with the observed rate based on a GW200115- and GW200105-like population. We note, however, that our binary population synthesis models in all cases predict a broader mass distribution compared

